LangGraph is designed for building stateful, controllable agent workflows, especially when an application needs multiple steps, loops, branching, persistence, or human approval.

Think:
LangChain = components

LangGraph = workflow/state orchestration

Example:

START
  ↓
Agent
  ↓
Should I use a tool?
 ↙        ↘
Yes       No
 ↓         ↓
Tool      Answer
 ↓
Agent
 ↓
END
Why LangGraph?

Useful for:

Agent loops
State management
Multi-agent workflows
Human approval
Retry mechanisms
Conditional routing
Long-running workflows
